as verified permission. Historical records are retained in qa/v19/HISTORICAL_NOTICE.txt.

V1.8–V1.9 replace the active globe and surface implementations, height-map shader,
geometry construction, picking, camera, display-data hooks, state mutations,
coordinate/ephemeris evaluation, horizon/disc sampling, raster lookup, visibility
series, regional finder, arrival ranking, observation controller and test adapters.
These replacements retain compatible public data/API contracts. They were written
after exposure to the reference source, not under a formally isolated clean-room process.
No claim of legally certified independence or competition eligibility is made.

Unused legacy showcase/vehicle/compass/export/camera implementations and external
source snapshots were removed. Existing LUNAR connected-base, DSN, Python science,
interface and education implementations remain. NASA/JPL ephemeris tables were
regenerated with engine/scripts/build_browser_ephemeris.py; metadata records hashes.

Prepared NASA-origin terrain/layer rasters, factual mission catalog records and
reference vectors were obtained through the referenced project and remain credited
as such. Their processing/provenance is not claimed as original LUNAR work.
Agreement with retained reference fixtures is regression evidence, not independent
scientific validation. NASA LOLA, LROC, SLDEM2015, Blue Marble, JPL SPICE/DE440 and
DSN sources remain in data metadata and scientific reports. Dependencies retain
licenses in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt. The LUNAR expedition craft/flag are illustrative.
OpenAI Codex assisted development and this rewrite.
